# TypeScript/React Coding Standards (Google Style Guide)

Follow Google's TypeScript style guide for all TypeScript and React code.

## Key Standards
- Use 2 spaces for indentation
- Maximum line length: 80 characters
- Use camelCase for variables, functions, and methods
- Use PascalCase for classes, interfaces, and components
- Use UPPER_SNAKE_CASE for constants
- Prefer `const` over `let`, avoid `var`
- Use semicolons at the end of statements
- Use single quotes for strings unless double quotes are needed

## Project Structure
The main frontend is in [frontend/](mdc:frontend/) with:
- Main application in [frontend/src/](mdc:frontend/src/)
- Components in [frontend/src/components/](mdc:frontend/src/components/)
- Services in [frontend/src/services/](mdc:frontend/src/services/)
- Hooks in [frontend/src/hooks/](mdc:frontend/src/hooks/)
- Types in [frontend/src/types/](mdc:frontend/src/types/)
- Store in [frontend/src/store/](mdc:frontend/src/store/)
- Tests in [frontend/src/__tests__/](mdc:frontend/src/__tests__/)
- Configuration in [frontend/package.json](mdc:frontend/package.json) and TypeScript config in [frontend/tsconfig.json](mdc:frontend/tsconfig.json)

## React/JSX Standards
- Use functional components with hooks
- Use PascalCase for component names
- Use camelCase for props
- Destructure props at the top of components
- Use TypeScript interfaces for prop types

## Tools
- Use ESLint with TypeScript rules (configured in [frontend/eslint.config.js](mdc:frontend/eslint.config.js))
- Use Prettier for code formatting (configured in [frontend/.prettierrc](mdc:frontend/.prettierrc))
- Use TypeScript strict mode

